# Hospital-Management-System
This is Hospital Management System web application that  allows Admins, Doctors, and Patients to interact with the system based on their roles.

Framework to use:
1) Flask for API
2) VueJS for UI
3) VueJS Advanced with CLI
4) Jinja2 templates if using CDN only for entry point
5) Bootstrap for HTML generation and Styling
6) SQLite for Databases
7) Redis for caching
8) Redis and Celery for batch jobs.


                                            Process of Making
# In Windows                                            

Created the Virtual environment in backend by using the code- "python -m venv myenv" in windows
Activating the virtual environment by using the code- ".\myenv\Scripts\Activate" in windows
Deactivate by using "deactivate"
Installing the flask by using the code- "pip3 install flask"
Installed the flask cors, in order to render out the data to specific link/path, by code- "pip install flask-cors"

Coming to Frontend, using Command Line Interface(CLI), I run-"npm create vue@latest"
Further I ran as recommended in the Terminal--

cd Hospital-project
npm install
npm run dev

Further import flask SQLAlchemy using command-"pip install flask-sqlalchemy"
Further import flask Security using command- "pip install flask-security"
Further install the flask CORS using the command- "pip install flask-cors"

# In WSL

1) Creating virtual environment in wsl by the code "source venv/bin/activate"
2) Installing Caching by the code "pip install Flask-Caching"
3) Install all the dependecies of the backend by the code "pip3 install -r requirement.txt"
4) Run the python server by code "python3 app.py"

### Next all four require to run Backend jobs- webhooks



5) Initilising redis server by the code "redis-server", if in order to vacate the redis server, use the code "sudo service redis-server stop".

## Option - 6 will run all the task of backend (task.py)
6) Initilising the celery worker server (In Virtual environment) by the code "celery -A app.celery worker --loglevel=info"

## Option-7 will enable the mailhog server
7) Initilising the Mailhog server by the command "mailhog"

## Option-8 will trigger the mail task
8) Initilising the celery beat server (In Virtual environment) by the command "celery -A app.celery beat --loglevel=info"

